<$TOP/mkfiles/mkfile.proto

O=k
CC=kc
LD=kl -H7 -M
AS=ka
AR=iar

CFLAGS=$CFLAGS_COMMON -I$TOP/include/arch/sparc

# claude: -M tells kl not to rewrite kc's generic AMUL/ADIV/ADIVL/AMOD/
# AMODL instructions into calls to software helpers (_mul/_div/_divl/
# _mod/_modl -- linkers/kl/noop.c's initmuldiv()), which this port has
# no implementation of anywhere. SPARC v8 (this backend's target) has
# real smul/sdiv/udiv hardware instructions and kl/asm.c's own opcode
# encoder (cases 52-55) already emits the correct sra+wry+div/mul
# sequence unconditionally -- -M just stops noop.c from swapping that
# real encoding out for a call in the first place. Needed once
# tests/c/mini2's fact()/fact_iter() (genuine variable multiply, not a
# compile-time constant Multab strength-reduction case) started
# linking: without it, kl fails "undefined: _mul" and friends.

# ARCHEXTRAOFILES: setjmp.s (setjmp()/longjmp(), needed unconditionally
# by os/linux/notify.c's own noted()) and vlop.s (_mulv, the 64-bit
# multiply helper compilers/cck/com64.c emits calls to) -- same pair
# power's own mkfile pulls in, see lib_core/libc/mkfile's own comment
# on this variable. rtsigaction.c is sparc's own hand-written
# _sysrtsigaction (5-arg kernel ABI, see syscall_linux_sparc.decl's
# comment); pipe.s is sparc's own hand-written _syspipe (register-pair
# return, not the pointer-argument shape mksyscall.sh generates, see
# that same decl file's comment) -- neither generated like every other
# arch's own syscall wrappers.
ARCHEXTRAOFILES=arch/sparc/setjmp.$O arch/sparc/vlop.$O arch/sparc/rtsigaction.$O arch/sparc/pipe.$O
